1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,676
April 14, 1912.

2
00:00:02,726 --> 00:00:03,888
The North Atlantic.

3
00:00:03,938 --> 00:00:06,306
It is 11:40 at night.

4
00:00:06,356 --> 00:00:11,530
Lookout Frederick Fleet sees a shadow in the darkness and rings the bell three times: Iceberg, right ahead!

5
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:18,238
Thirty-seven seconds later, the largest passenger ship in the world scrapes along the ice.

6
00:00:18,288 --> 00:00:22,307
This is the story of the Titanic's last two hours and forty minutes.

7
00:00:25,357 --> 00:00:29,746
Four days earlier, the Titanic had set off from Southampton in front of the crowds.

8
00:00:29,796 --> 00:00:32,705
There were more than 2,200 people on board.

9
00:00:32,755 --> 00:00:37,613
It had luxurious dining saloons, a gymnasium and long promenade decks.

10
00:00:37,663 --> 00:00:41,676
But the lifeboats could hold at most 1,178 people.

11
00:00:41,726 --> 00:00:46,391
That day, the wireless room received six ice warnings from other ships.

12
00:00:46,441 --> 00:00:50,679
Wireless operator Jack Phillips was struggling to keep up with passengers' messages.

13
00:00:50,729 --> 00:00:56,476
Around 11 p.m., he cut off the last warning and told the sender to shut up.

14
00:00:56,526 --> 00:01:02,402
Half an hour later, the wireless operator of the nearby Californian switched off his set and went to bed.

15
00:01:02,452 --> 00:01:07,088
The iceberg opened at least five watertight compartments on the ship's right side.

16
00:01:07,138 --> 00:01:11,572
The Titanic was built to stay afloat with no more than four compartments flooded.

17
00:01:11,622 --> 00:01:15,003
The ship's fate was sealed within minutes.

18
00:01:15,053 --> 00:01:19,456
After midnight, distress calls began pouring out of the wireless room.

19
00:01:19,506 --> 00:01:22,598
At a quarter to one, the first lifeboat was lowered.

20
00:01:22,648 --> 00:01:26,236
The boat, built for sixty-five, carried only twenty-six people.

21
00:01:26,286 --> 00:01:30,352
Because most people did not believe this giant ship could sink.

22
00:01:30,402 --> 00:01:35,459
The ship's musicians kept playing on deck to calm the passengers.

23
00:01:35,509 --> 00:01:38,870
Captain Edward Smith stayed with his ship to the end.

24
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:44,416
Around two o'clock, the bow sank completely under water.

25
00:01:44,466 --> 00:01:47,578
The stern rose into the air, the lights went out and the ship broke in two.

26
00:01:47,628 --> 00:01:54,124
At 2:20, only the lifeboats remained on the surface, along with hundreds of people struggling in the freezing water.

27
00:01:54,173 --> 00:01:56,808
The water temperature was minus two degrees Celsius.

28
00:01:56,858 --> 00:02:01,519
The distress call was picked up by the Carpathia, about a hundred kilometres away.

29
00:02:01,569 --> 00:02:06,150
Captain Arthur Rostron drove his ship at full speed through the ice.

30
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:09,163
At ten past four in the morning, it reached the first lifeboat.

31
00:02:09,213 --> 00:02:11,134
705 people were rescued.

32
00:02:11,184 --> 00:02:14,157
More than 1,500 never came back.

33
00:02:14,207 --> 00:02:19,557
Three days later, when the Carpathia reached New York, thousands were waiting at the pier.

34
00:02:19,607 --> 00:02:24,045
The shipping company's office filled with people desperate for news of their loved ones.

35
00:02:24,095 --> 00:02:30,520
The newsboys all carried one headline: Titanic disaster, great loss of life.

36
00:02:30,570 --> 00:02:33,434
The Titanic stayed lost for seventy-three years.

37
00:02:33,484 --> 00:02:37,713
In 1985 it was found nearly four kilometres deep.

38
00:02:37,764 --> 00:02:41,496
Today its rusting hull decays a little more every year.

39
00:02:41,546 --> 00:02:44,364
What do you think was the biggest mistake that night?

40
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:47,922
Ignoring the ice warnings, too few lifeboats, or the Californian switching off its radio?

41
00:02:47,972 --> 00:02:50,658
Tell us in the comments.

42
00:02:50,708 --> 00:02:51,954
I'm Kismet Stories.

43
00:02:52,004 --> 00:02:55,906
See you in the next story.
